# RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md is committed with each release on purpose: CI reads
# it to build the announcement. The tag annotation cannot be trusted for
# that, because actions/checkout lands the tag as a lightweight ref and
# `git tag -l --format=%(contents)` then falls back to the commit message.
